From 5eaee979b916d81772f40b90487d2d53089bf68a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:25:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] RomM Library: add "Delete from the SD card" to the game
 screen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Requested: when a downloaded ROM is broken or does not work, it could not be removed from the
RomM menu.

- game screen: "Excluir do cartão SD" appears when the game is on the card; confirmation (A/B)
  that shows up to 3 names, the count of the rest and the total size, and says saves and save
  states are NOT deleted. Menu numbering adapts; without the game on the card nothing changes.
- every successful download now writes Data/romm/dl/<id>.lst ("folder<TAB>item"), also for
  multi-file games (ZIP extracted; each moved item is recorded, partial extractions included), so
  only what the app downloaded is deleted.
- single-file games downloaded before the lists existed are recognised by path.
- safety: empty/./../slash-containing names are never deleted, an item listed by another game is
  kept, nothing outside Roms/ is touched; also removes that game's .rommpart/.state and the
  folder's *_cache*.db so it disappears from the emulator list.
- game list marks multi-file games already on the card with "* " too.
- tests: 124 -> 159 checks (single, multi-file, cancel, legacy, shared item, dangerous list
  entries, saves untouched). README and docs/HISTORICO-2026-11-22.md (section 11) updated.

Only simulated here (dash, mawk); not run on the device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
